[{:db/id 17592186119820 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4f44c2f3-4f54-5e93-a6f8-f1e6cfd5ee6a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119631 :question/problem "Find the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ if $\\,\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ and\n![](images/79/798c2f477907d0d3414eeed0a2f37871c69466d9b4a098699a364f6a034c0679.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,\\mathcal{B}.$ Since we are told that ![](images/de/de91d9b4cd4eabed0a27696d7bf0512c19f6c66eb3c81ab6dc6a73fc0a1c15a5.svg) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(-1)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119859 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d9b245f0-31aa-56fe-aa26-5663dd9e140f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119674 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](images/20/2060371fae8253c2f26c54e53032526c1b1514f282dde33c09657810ed9a6bb7.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n![](images/f7/f778bc04188da8bf824aab34f770f555a01ceabcc0153afd557577f1c8b14414.svg)\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = (-5) \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_1 + 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_2\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n![](images/cd/cd3c27c4e964d5f4f1f9cf2c1fd5f91c6ba188b58aad1ef9388ba8faf7f03618.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119821 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-893314bd-9641-54d7-a9c3-9945a815ea4f" "question-ebceb075-efc9-5bc0-95d2-77852526cbc8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119632 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](images/c3/c36abdf2587e3b457ef47d67b3df21d7b8de505202e4bc1f4629e3284c49b87b.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n![](images/e5/e5b57b4f1488c927d64d89cb4352715b471025a111a39fe786c869973401fbd4.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix above corresponds to the following system of equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2 =-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1 + 3 \\left( -1 \\right)  = -5\n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad\nx_1 = -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/28/286b19d6c3b5b3fac7f65ffd4adab1b175d4dab5fab1e5bb7a85da692f09224a.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119822 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ec45397c-5ced-5a47-b9a9-86c6aa1d1bf3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119633 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\},$ where\n![](images/5d/5d9d3780a503745f072cdb2e9cea0eedddca811143b05a2cc426480e93c8dac9.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above system as an augmented matrix $M$ and reducing using Gaussian elimination, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -9{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=7 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3}=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 =2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-9x_2 - 2 = 7 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_2=-1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+3(-1) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1 = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/76/766d220a3c5bc2819ab05886751b6a1b782ece06c9d71b9baaaee19e9a2ecbdd.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-4f44c2f3-4f54-5e93-a6f8-f1e6cfd5ee6a" :question/id #uuid "4f44c2f3-4f54-5e93-a6f8-f1e6cfd5ee6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-35222" :question/problem "Find the vector $x$, if $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,5\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]= \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e4638b53-3685-5dc3-a202-7169b92a21b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e4638b53-3685-5dc3-a202-7169b92a21b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4638b53-3685-5dc3-a202-7169b92a21b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fd15848a-b716-582c-9c1d-7cd0b9bfb17f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd15848a-b716-582c-9c1d-7cd0b9bfb17f" "answer-aae52088-4930-599a-9ee5-fd6a528c248d" "answer-64a1f0ad-84e2-58dd-a8ed-11320d5d0931" "answer-d298d01b-b978-5454-a811-dd683962843e" "answer-65c3f0eb-5935-5403-8987-9332ba2a913e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd15848a-b716-582c-9c1d-7cd0b9bfb17f" :answer/id #uuid "fd15848a-b716-582c-9c1d-7cd0b9bfb17f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aae52088-4930-599a-9ee5-fd6a528c248d" :answer/id #uuid "aae52088-4930-599a-9ee5-fd6a528c248d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-21 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64a1f0ad-84e2-58dd-a8ed-11320d5d0931" :answer/id #uuid "64a1f0ad-84e2-58dd-a8ed-11320d5d0931" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-21 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d298d01b-b978-5454-a811-dd683962843e" :answer/id #uuid "d298d01b-b978-5454-a811-dd683962843e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65c3f0eb-5935-5403-8987-9332ba2a913e" :answer/id #uuid "65c3f0eb-5935-5403-8987-9332ba2a913e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d9b245f0-31aa-56fe-aa26-5663dd9e140f" :question/id #uuid "d9b245f0-31aa-56fe-aa26-5663dd9e140f" :question/math-academy-id "q-112211" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,-8\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-7\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=(-8)\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-7)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fe323417-1cf2-5a08-b6a1-9d36f7d769a5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe323417-1cf2-5a08-b6a1-9d36f7d769a5" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe323417-1cf2-5a08-b6a1-9d36f7d769a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-60013665-0a5a-5449-9017-6cb6ae7ed2ca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60013665-0a5a-5449-9017-6cb6ae7ed2ca" "answer-ba977b58-8add-5c57-ae69-640a36ab4ef9" "answer-2115aac5-da66-5510-8b11-176ba754f81a" "answer-45dbc0e6-16a9-5c62-a183-2dd30e767a3a" "answer-7ad6f309-f775-5604-ba46-fa9609a5688b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60013665-0a5a-5449-9017-6cb6ae7ed2ca" :answer/id #uuid "60013665-0a5a-5449-9017-6cb6ae7ed2ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba977b58-8add-5c57-ae69-640a36ab4ef9" :answer/id #uuid "ba977b58-8add-5c57-ae69-640a36ab4ef9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2115aac5-da66-5510-8b11-176ba754f81a" :answer/id #uuid "2115aac5-da66-5510-8b11-176ba754f81a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45dbc0e6-16a9-5c62-a183-2dd30e767a3a" :answer/id #uuid "45dbc0e6-16a9-5c62-a183-2dd30e767a3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ad6f309-f775-5604-ba46-fa9609a5688b" :answer/id #uuid "7ad6f309-f775-5604-ba46-fa9609a5688b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-893314bd-9641-54d7-a9c3-9945a815ea4f" :question/id #uuid "893314bd-9641-54d7-a9c3-9945a815ea4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-112246" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-14 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=8.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(8)=-14\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-6)+8=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c1adc025-e35c-5c7f-b3d2-a22f6c131b32"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c1adc025-e35c-5c7f-b3d2-a22f6c131b32" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1adc025-e35c-5c7f-b3d2-a22f6c131b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd67ec1c-d0b6-583a-93ea-2320fc866ee8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bd67ec1c-d0b6-583a-93ea-2320fc866ee8" "answer-d730889c-d211-5f79-808d-edb05582ebf9" "answer-8c55afca-aada-59e7-8566-a67479e5ca90" "answer-19ab819f-c33e-5cef-9c7d-94cc01a08eea" "answer-67fe8fd6-4155-5cce-93e6-650aa08ca771"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd67ec1c-d0b6-583a-93ea-2320fc866ee8" :answer/id #uuid "bd67ec1c-d0b6-583a-93ea-2320fc866ee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d730889c-d211-5f79-808d-edb05582ebf9" :answer/id #uuid "d730889c-d211-5f79-808d-edb05582ebf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c55afca-aada-59e7-8566-a67479e5ca90" :answer/id #uuid "8c55afca-aada-59e7-8566-a67479e5ca90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19ab819f-c33e-5cef-9c7d-94cc01a08eea" :answer/id #uuid "19ab819f-c33e-5cef-9c7d-94cc01a08eea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67fe8fd6-4155-5cce-93e6-650aa08ca771" :answer/id #uuid "67fe8fd6-4155-5cce-93e6-650aa08ca771" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ebceb075-efc9-5bc0-95d2-77852526cbc8" :question/id #uuid "ebceb075-efc9-5bc0-95d2-77852526cbc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-112251" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -38 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -38 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -38 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 24\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -38 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -19 & -38 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -19 & -38 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{12}{19}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -19 & -38 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -19{x}_{2}=-38.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-5(2)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=10+2=12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ea7b226f-79df-5fde-bf3b-18e9fc4ba990"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea7b226f-79df-5fde-bf3b-18e9fc4ba990" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea7b226f-79df-5fde-bf3b-18e9fc4ba990" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-71804a18-d46f-54b8-91e7-a3197dfed1f6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fcb18c3c-3fae-5461-a45e-727641240832" "answer-56a6c136-0c09-5ee6-8667-b8c578a8d106" "answer-71804a18-d46f-54b8-91e7-a3197dfed1f6" "answer-60f7a927-bdd2-5f05-8617-e8e1e2381233" "answer-ca4c5e51-eb69-5a8f-82a6-2590266e47b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcb18c3c-3fae-5461-a45e-727641240832" :answer/id #uuid "fcb18c3c-3fae-5461-a45e-727641240832" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56a6c136-0c09-5ee6-8667-b8c578a8d106" :answer/id #uuid "56a6c136-0c09-5ee6-8667-b8c578a8d106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71804a18-d46f-54b8-91e7-a3197dfed1f6" :answer/id #uuid "71804a18-d46f-54b8-91e7-a3197dfed1f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60f7a927-bdd2-5f05-8617-e8e1e2381233" :answer/id #uuid "60f7a927-bdd2-5f05-8617-e8e1e2381233" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca4c5e51-eb69-5a8f-82a6-2590266e47b5" :answer/id #uuid "ca4c5e51-eb69-5a8f-82a6-2590266e47b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ec45397c-5ced-5a47-b9a9-86c6aa1d1bf3" :question/id #uuid "ec45397c-5ced-5a47-b9a9-86c6aa1d1bf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-76073" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ \\,\\,-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ \\,\\,0=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the third equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a79bee7d-12b6-5017-ae13-ca00a861bd24"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a79bee7d-12b6-5017-ae13-ca00a861bd24" :answer-field/id #uuid "a79bee7d-12b6-5017-ae13-ca00a861bd24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a5ba42a7-b00b-5980-9f89-48160c1eb49e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d13c159c-f442-5933-a821-d94880c3ba32" "answer-0470cd3b-2bcb-575e-9def-d43004406207" "answer-eec553dd-6fd7-5208-9292-850213e9c19b" "answer-a3e208c3-ba1a-51ec-b367-c2784fabe06c" "answer-a5ba42a7-b00b-5980-9f89-48160c1eb49e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d13c159c-f442-5933-a821-d94880c3ba32" :answer/id #uuid "d13c159c-f442-5933-a821-d94880c3ba32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0470cd3b-2bcb-575e-9def-d43004406207" :answer/id #uuid "0470cd3b-2bcb-575e-9def-d43004406207" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eec553dd-6fd7-5208-9292-850213e9c19b" :answer/id #uuid "eec553dd-6fd7-5208-9292-850213e9c19b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3e208c3-ba1a-51ec-b367-c2784fabe06c" :answer/id #uuid "a3e208c3-ba1a-51ec-b367-c2784fabe06c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5ba42a7-b00b-5980-9f89-48160c1eb49e" :answer/id #uuid "a5ba42a7-b00b-5980-9f89-48160c1eb49e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121042 :tutorial/content "Given a subspace $H$ with a basis $\\mathcal B = \\{ \\mathbf b_1, \\mathbf b_2 \\}$ and a vector $\\mathbf x \\in H,$ the **coordinates of the vector** $\\mathbf{x}$ **relative to the basis** $\\mathcal{B}$ are the coefficients ${\\color{red} x_1}$ and ${\\color{blue} x_2}$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}x_1} \\mathbf{b}_1+{\\color{blue}x_2} \\mathbf{b}_2 = \\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nWe can write the vector $\\mathbf x$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal B$ using these coordinates, as follows:\n\n![](images/05/0593ca6a838b66c4623e8749eb5236d6259b1f9bf36ed0d68b83c49781076341.svg)\n\nTo demonstrate, consider the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where \n\n![](images/f3/f355faa0c477775f2a1cbb3522d0743cdbc9649a5ee9c55b579b1fac9ae2a661.svg)\n\nAlso let $H = \\textrm{span} \\{ \\mathbf b_1, \\mathbf b_2 \\},$ and consider the vector ![](images/78/78357fcf51c9cd6b7873f5bc35fcc214cb3790bcec00ee69d0932f15aacd39cb.svg)\n\nThe vector $\\mathbf x$ can be expressed as a unique linear combination of $\\mathbf b_1$ and $\\mathbf b_2.$ That is to say, there exist *unique coefficients* $\\color{red}x_1$ and $\\color{blue}x_2$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's solve for these coefficients. From the above, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of this system is \n\n![](images/82/82d4f494936d23e9b697aa4518edf68f7ea62e504d9d2576a6d13971acaf1c96.svg)\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = {\\color{red}3} \\mathbf{b}_1+ {\\color{blue}2} \\mathbf{b}_2,\n$$\n\nwhich can be visualized as shown below.\n\n![](images/94/94b2934727a32284e9790e59ccd301bd858a0258843314a2968285a5eda7a302.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121066 :tutorial/content "Let's consider a set of vectors\n![](images/0d/0d78e1b2d01003885882f19b3856278e5024719f26f33594fd071fbd73273b71.svg)\n\nNotice that the set $\\mathcal{S}$ is linearly independent since the vector equation $x_1\\mathbf{e}_1+x_2\\mathbf{e}_2+x_3\\mathbf{e}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ leads to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has only the zero solution. \n\nAlso, notice that any vector in $\\mathbb{R}^3$ can be written as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{e}_1,$ $\\mathbf{e}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{e}_3.$ For instance,\n![](images/ef/ef28dd8cbad6d256b9fa82c487263af3327ce630839cfcd1c7433417d0e0ae73.svg)\n\nIn particular, the equation above tells us that \n![](images/72/724f42afb534edbde7588c5508a4bf8de6d3cd068bc2989da7c7207b1bf7a1ba.svg)\nthat is to say, the numbers $\\color{red}-2,$ $\\color{red}0,$ $\\color{red}5$ are the coordinates of $\\mathbf{v}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{S}.$ \n\nThe basis $\\mathcal{S}$ is somewhat special, since the coordinates of a vector relative to this basis coincide with the components of the vector. We refer to $\\mathcal{S}$ as the **standard basis**. Remember that in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and $\\mathbb{R}^3$ we even have special notations for the vectors of the standard basis:\n![](images/ae/aee5dd3226ebe950defc8b873399a884e0679ce701a3a55354ef01960e029f8e.svg)\n\n![](images/dd/dd96e0b70173adf8983feb4975c351ab3e417c34ed4a6a944bc391e33db4c8e9.png)\n\nIn general, the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ is\n\n![](images/a8/a8e4b648898c0dc036e228fb84945833dc40c053beff034596e098c4dd077e23.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120054 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
